{"attachment_metadata":[],"author_person_id":"merlini-2","author_source_handle":"@GobRoss","content_sha256":"8a3d638926f1a38e373ab62208f7c478fd88a8e8e45810ade92f7affb6ad4a4d","created_at":"2026-09-01T09:01:26Z","english_summary":null,"ingested_at":"2026-09-01T09:01:30.891742Z","record_id":"tg:tawg:3866","relations":[{"relation_type":"reply_to","target_record_id":"tg:tawg:16"}],"schema_version":"tawg.source-record.v1","source_locator":"repo:data/telegram/2026/09/messages.jsonl#tg:tawg:3866","source_payload":{"author_is_bot":false,"edited":true,"message_kind":"group_message","message_thread_id":16,"update_id":998811144},"source_type":"telegram_message","text_original":"Confirmed your diagnosis, and thanks for the clean preflight. Production is a pre-TSEI build — the\n/tsei/profile-a router 404s on every path including an unauthenticated POST (would be 401 if it were merely\nfail-closed on the missing secret), so the route isn’t in the running code at all. The be2fd43f merge never\ndeployed: no Railway auto-deploy hook was configured.\n\nTwo version things I hit while diagnosing, both worth fixing before we deploy so the receipt is legible:\nthe TSEI gateway (#5–#8) landed without a version bump — old prod and be2fd43f both report 0.7.0, so\n/health can’t tell them apart, which is exactly what hid the stale deploy. And the lockfile’s own version\nhad drifted to 0.6.5 while package.json was 0.7.0. I opened [#9] — npm version minor → 0.8.0,\nresyncing the lockfile; version labels only, dependency tree untouched, so your 97/97 and the image build are\nunaffected.\n\nWe own the Railway project. Proposed sequence: you review/merge #9, then I deploy that merge commit\n(a legibly-0.8.0, TSEI build) to ccip-router-production with a dedicated TSEI_PROFILE_A_INGEST_SECRET\n(fresh, ≥32, distinct from ADMIN_SECRET — your mutation test rejects reuse anyway; secret goes straight\ninto Railway, never through chat), and fix the auto-deploy hook so this doesn’t recur. If you’d rather I deploy\nthe literal be2fd43f instead and bump separately, say so — but a legibly-versioned build seems better for the\nreceipt.\n\nI’ll ping you the moment /tsei/profile-a/observations is live (non-404) so you can run the production smoke\ntest and submit the public TSEI receipt. Happy to add you to the Railway project for self-serve future deploys\ntoo — say the word.","updated_at":"2026-09-01T09:08:54Z"}
